1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,500
EchoPath maximizes Slicer with the public chest CT already loaded.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:13,000
EchoPath changes the axial slice position and checks the updated cross-section.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,500
EchoPath uses Slicer’s module selector to reach Volume Rendering.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,500
The same GUI workflow runs inside a specialized desktop application.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,500
The CT stays visible in the axial, coronal and sagittal views.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,000
EchoPath opens the available volume-rendering methods.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
VTK CPU Ray Casting is selected for this software-rendered VM.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,500
EchoPath turns on volume visibility in the 3D view.

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,500
Slicer’s preset gallery supplies the CT-Bone display settings.

10
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,500
EchoPath selects the bone preset while retaining the three slice views.

11
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,500
The rendered chest appears alongside the linked CT slice views.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,500
EchoPath opens Slicer’s Save Scene and Unsaved Data dialog.

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,000
The scene can be exported together with its data as one bundle.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
EchoPath selects Medical Reality Bundle (.mrb).

15
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,500
The output stays in the local Windows VM.

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,000
EchoPath selects the prepared EchoPath-Slicer-Demo directory.

17
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Slicer will write the bundle beside the sample-data files.

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
EchoPath edits the scene filename through the Save dialog.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The output is CTChest-demo-2026-10-12.mrb.

20
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The filename, destination and bundle format are set.

21
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,500
EchoPath clicks Save and waits for Slicer to package the scene.

22
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:17,500
Three CT slice views and the CT-Bone rendering remain visible after export.
